Column name: Capture_Area Type: TEXT Description: Area (or Capture Area) - One of the either four or two active regions where tissue can be placed on a Visium slide. Each area is intended to contain only one tissue sample. Slide areas are named consecutively from top to bottom: A1, B1, C1, D1 for Visium slides with 6.5 mm Capture Area and A, B for CytAssist slides with 11 mm Capture Area. Both CytAssist slides with 6.5 mm Capture Area and Gateway Slides contain only two slide areas, A1 and D1.
Column name: HTAN_Parent_Data_File_ID Type: TEXT Description: HTAN Data File Identifier indicating the file(s) from which these files were derived
Column name: Run_ID Type: TEXT Description: A unique identifier for this individual run (typically associated with a single slide) of the spatial transcriptomic processing workflow.
Column name: Mean_Reads_per_Spatial_Spot Type: TEXT Description: The number of reads, both under and outside of tissue, divided by the number of barcodes associated with a spot under tissue.
Column name: Data_Release Type: TEXT Description: Inclusion in HTAN Data Release e.g. Release 1.0
Column name: Filename Type: TEXT Description: Name of a file
Column name: HTAN_Center Type: TEXT Description: Name of HTAN Center e.g. HTAN HTAPP
Column name: Visium_File_Type Type: TEXT Description: The file type generated for the visium experiment.
Column name: HTAN_Parent_Biospecimen_ID Type: TEXT Description: HTAN Biospecimen Identifier (eg HTANx_yyy_zzz) indicating the biospecimen(s) from which these files were derived; multiple parent biospecimen should be comma-separated
Column name: Manifest_Version Type: NUMBER Description: Latest version of metadata manifest
Column name: Median_Number_Genes_per_Spatial_Spot Type: TEXT Description: The median number of genes detected per spot under tissue-associated barcode. Detection is defined as the presence of at least 1 UMI count.
Column name: Proportion_Reads_Mapped_to_Transcriptome Type: TEXT Description: Fraction of reads that mapped to a unique gene in the transcriptome. The read must be consistent with annotated splice junctions. These reads are considered for UMI counting.
Column name: Spots_under_tissue Type: TEXT Description: The number of barcodes associated with a spot under tissue.
Column name: entityId Type: TEXT Description: Synapse ID of entity
Column name: Sequencing_Saturation Type: TEXT Description: The fraction of reads originating from an already-observed UMI. This is a function of library complexity and sequencing depth. More specifically, this is the fraction of confidently mapped, valid spot-barcode, valid UMI reads that had a non-unique (spot-barcode, UMI, gene).
Column name: Workflow_Link Type: TEXT Description: Link to workflow or command. DockStore.org recommended. URL
Column name: Id Type: TEXT Description: Unique identifier of entity e.g. a96059eb-81af-4b24-ae50-9242c0d8f819
Column name: Proportion_Reads_Mapped Type: TEXT Description: Proportion of mapped reads collected from samtools. Number
Column name: File_Size Type: NUMBER Description: Size of file (bucket object) in bytes
Column name: md5 Type: TEXT Description: md5 hash of file
Column name: HTAN_Data_File_ID Type: TEXT Description: Self-identifier for this data file - HTAN ID of this file HTAN ID SOP (eg HTANx_yyy_zzz)
Column name: Workflow_Version Type: TEXT Description: Major version of the workflow (e.g. Cell Ranger v3.1)
Column name: File_Format Type: TEXT Description: Format of a file (e.g. txt, csv, fastq, bam, etc.)
Column name: Manifest_Id Type: TEXT Description: Synapse ID of manifest containing file annotation
Column name: CDS_Release Type: TEXT Description: CDS transfer package in which file was included e.g. v22.6.1.seq
Column name: Component Type: TEXT Description: Category of metadata (e.g. Diagnosis, Biospecimen, scRNA-seq Level 1, etc.); provide the same one for all items/rows.
Column name: Median_UMI_Counts_per_Spot Type: TEXT Description: The median number of UMI counts per tissue covered spot.
