Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant columns and their potential use  
• "Run_ID": primary filter to locate all records that belong to the specific Visium / spatial‑transcriptomics run ‘HT264P1‑S1H2Fc2U1Z1Bs1‑H2Bs2‑Test’.  
• "Filename": required in the result set – name/path of the file.  
• "HTAN_Parent_Biospecimen_ID": required in the result set – parent biospecimen(s).  
• "Component": required in the result set – identifies the metadata level + assay type (e.g. Level1 vs Level3).  
• "File_Format": required in the result set – file‑type (fastq, bam, h5ad …).  
• "entityId": required in the result set – Synapse identifier of the file row.  
• Conditions – either  
 – exact match → WHERE "Run_ID" = 'HT264P1‑S1H2Fc2U1Z1Bs1‑H2Bs2‑Test'  
 – fuzzy search on other tables that lack "Run_ID", e.g. WHERE "Filename" ILIKE '%HT264P1%H2Bs2%'  

Below are ten exploratory Snowflake SQL queries (simple → complex) that can be run to retrieve and consolidate the requested metadata.  
All column and object names are double‑quoted, every query limits to 20 rows for safety.

```sql
-- 1. Level‑1 Visium FASTQ/Lane files for the run
SELECT
  "Filename",
  "HTAN_Parent_Biospecimen_ID",
  "Component",
  "File_Format",
  "entityId",
  "Run_ID"
FROM "HTAN_2"."HTAN"."_10XVISIUM_SPATIALTRANSCRIPTOMICS_SCRNASEQ_LEVEL1_METADATA_CURRENT"
WHERE "Run_ID" = 'HT264P1-S1H2Fc2U1Z1Bs1-H2Bs2-Test'
LIMIT 20;
```

